<title>LUXEMBOURG: ATHLETICS-EUROCROSS CROSS-COUNTRY RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-EUROCROSS CROSS-COUNTRY RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>DIEKIRCH, Luxembourg 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results from</p>
<p>Sunday's Reebok Eurocross cross-country athletics meeting, ninth</p>
<p>round of the IAAF World Cross Challenge series:</p>
<p>Men (10.2 km)</p>
<p> 1. Bernard Barmasai (Kenya)	  30 minutes 41 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Mohammed Mourit (Morocco)		   30:43</p>
<p> 3. Dieter Baumann (Germany)		    30:59</p>
<p> 4. Robert Stefko (Slovakia)		    31:12</p>
<p> 5. Jonah Koech (Kenya)			   31:17</p>
<p> 6. Kamiel Maase (Netherlands)		  31:20</p>
<p> 7. David Kipruto (Kenya)			 31:30</p>
<p> 8. Tom Van Hooste (Belgium)		    31:39</p>
<p> 9. Reda Benzine (Algeria)			31:44</p>
<p> 10. Eric Bouffioux (Belgium)		   31:47</p>
<p>Women (4.8 km)</p>
<p> 1. Elena Fidatov (Romania)		     15:50</p>
<p> 2. Anita Weyermann (Switzerland)	     15:52</p>
<p> 3. Colleen de Reuck (South Africa)	   16:02</p>
<p> 4. Lucy Elliott (Britain)			16:16</p>
<p> 5. Ioana Olteanu (Romania)		     16:25</p>
<p> 6. Marleen Renders (Belgium)		   16:33</p>
<p> 7. Joyce Chepchumba (Kenya)		    16:37</p>
<p> 8. Stefanija Statkuviene (Lithuania)	 16:38</p>
<p> 9. Anne-Marie Danneels (Belgium)	     16:41</p>
<p> 10. Irma Heeran (Netherlands)		  16:44</p>
<p>leading standings after nine rounds:</p>
<p>Men</p>
<p> 1. Barmasai				 72 points</p>
<p> 2. Keith Cullen (Britain)	     67</p>
<p> 3. Stefko				   65</p>
<p> 4. Paulo Guerra (Portugal)	    63</p>
<p> 5. Yann Millon (France)		 58</p>
<p>Women</p>
<p> 1. Fidatov				  100 points</p>
<p> 2. Gete Wami (Ethiopia)		 88</p>
<p> 3. Elliott				  65</p>
<p> 4  Iulia Negura (Romania)	     62</p>
<p> 5. De Reuck				 57</p>
<p>Note: Negura is currently suspended from competition pending</p>
<p>a hearing after producing a positive drug test.</p>
